 "viz_about_hdr": {
 "type": "splunk.markdown",
 "options": {
 "fontColor": "#049FD9",
 "fontSize": "small",
 "markdown": "## About \u2014 Metrics Reference"
 }
 },
 "viz_about_body": {
 "type": "splunk.markdown",
 "options": {
 "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
 "fontColor": "#000000",
 "fontSize": "small",
 "markdown": "## About this dashboard\n\n**Cisco Spaces \u2014 Intelligence** answers six questions the customer cares about during and around an emergency-management exercise (Op Florida Ready):\n\n1. **Are the buildings comfortable?** (Environmental Intelligence)\n2. **Are we close to capacity?** (Capacity & Prediction)\n3. **Which rooms get used and which are wasted?** (Room Utilization)\n4. **Did the network handle the surge?** (Activation Readiness)\n5. **Who actually showed up \u2014 staff vs guests, repeats vs first-timers?** (Visitor Intelligence)\n6. **Did the wireless network's user experience hold up?** (Network Impact)\n\nThe dashboard cross-correlates **Cisco Spaces firehose** (people-count and presence telemetry from APs), **Cisco Catalyst Center / DNAC** (network-side health) and **Webex device telemetry** (in-room temperature & humidity sensors) to tell one coherent story.\n\n---\n\n## Data sources\n\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose \u2014 DEVICE_COUNT** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\"`) \u2014 `deviceCounts.userCount`, `associatedCount`, `deviceCount`, `estimatedCapacityPercentage`, location hierarchy. Filtered to floor scope (`inferredLocationTypes=FLOOR`) for per-floor panels, BUILDING scope for the campus map.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose \u2014 DEVICE_ASSOCIATION** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_ASSOCIATION\" event=\"ASSOCIATE\"`) \u2014 `device.macAddress`, `ssid`. Powers unique-visitor / repeat-visitor / SSID composition.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose \u2014 DEVICE_PRESENCE** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\"`) \u2014 `macAddress`, `location.inferredLocationTypes`. Used for inter-campus traveler analysis (Sankey).\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose \u2014 SPACE_OCCUPANCY** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"SPACE_OCCUPANCY\"`) \u2014 `space.name`, `space.capacity`, `peakPeopleCount`, `peoplePresence`. Used by the Room Utilization tab.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose \u2014 WEBEX_TELEMETRY** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\"`) \u2014 `ambientTemp`, `relativeHumidity`, `deviceInfo.serialNumber`.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 networkhealth** (`cisco:dnac:networkhealth`) \u2014 overall network health score (0-100) per category.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 clienthealth** (`cisco:dnac:clienthealth`) \u2014 overall client health score (0-100) by client type.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 client** (`cisco:dnac:client`) \u2014 per-client health, RSSI, SSID, band, onboarding time, site hierarchy.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 devicehealth** (`cisco:dnac:devicehealth`) \u2014 per-AP health, CPU/memory utilization, issue count, reachability, manageability.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 issue** (`cisco:dnac:issue`) \u2014 active DNAC issues with priority + site.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center \u2014 compliance** (`cisco:dnac:compliance`) \u2014 per-device compliance status.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 1 \u2014 Environmental Intelligence\n\n- **Avg temperature / Avg humidity** \u2014 mean across all Webex room sensors over the selected time range. Temperature converted Celsius \u2192 Fahrenheit via `temp_f = round(temp*9/5+32, 2)`.\n- **Current sensor readings** \u2014 latest temp + humidity per Webex device, with a comfort verdict: `Optimal` if 68-76 \u00b0F and 30-60 % RH; otherwise `Warm/Humid` or `Cool/Dry`.\n- **Temperature / Humidity by floor + exercise annotations** \u2014 hourly average per device, with vertical markers for the three Op Florida Ready dates pulled from the shared `ds_annotations` saved search.\n- **Spaces \u00d7 Webex \u2014 occupancy + temperature overlay** \u2014 hourly occupancy (`deviceCounts.userCount`) as columns, hourly temperature as overlay line. Visual answer to \"do crowds heat the room?\"\n- **Spaces \u00d7 Webex \u2014 people vs. temperature scatter** \u2014 one dot per hour. Upward slope = thermal-load correlation.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 2 \u2014 Capacity & Prediction\n\n- **Peak users today** \u2014 max value of `max(users) by _time, floor` in the period (busiest hour on busiest floor).\n- **Avg users (period)** \u2014 mean of those hourly per-floor maxima \u2014 your \"typical concurrent population\" baseline.\n- **Highest / Second-highest capacity floor (period peak)** \u2014 per-floor max of `deviceCounts.estimatedCapacityPercentage` over the window, scoped to the two specific buildings.\n- **Users by city over time** \u2014 hourly peak `userCount` summed across all floors of a city.\n- **Occupancy forecast (24-hour prediction)** \u2014 Splunk `predict` on the hourly user-count series, projecting 24 h forward with 95 % confidence band.\n- **Capacity % by floor over time** \u2014 hourly max `estimatedCapacityPercentage` per floor; `useother=t` keeps the top 10 floors visible.\n- **This week vs last week** \u2014 hourly user count split by `if(_time >= now()-7d, \"This Week\", \"Last Week\")`.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 3 \u2014 Room Utilization\n\nSource: `cisco:spaces:firehose eventType=SPACE_OCCUPANCY`. Each event reports a room, its capacity, peak headcount, and a presence flag.\n\n- **Total rooms** \u2014 `dc(spaceOccupancy.space.name)` (distinct rooms reporting any data).\n- **Ghost rooms** \u2014 rooms where `presence!=\"OCCUPIED\" AND people==0` for \u2265 80 % of all observations in the window. Effectively never used.\n- **Hot rooms** \u2014 rooms where `avg(peakPeopleCount) / capacity \u2265 0.8`. Persistently overloaded.\n- **Rooms by utilization tier (pie)** \u2014 tiers from `avg(peakPeopleCount)/capacity`: Hot (\u2265 80 %), Active (40-80 %), Idle (< 40 %), Empty (\u2248 0).\n- **Top 15 rooms by utilization** \u2014 bar chart sorted by `avg(peakPeopleCount)/capacity * 100`.\n- **Room utilization detail** \u2014 full table: building, floor, room, capacity, avg/peak utilization %, time-occupied %, report count.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 4 \u2014 Activation Readiness\n\nTells the \"did the network survive Op Florida Ready\" story. The activation window is configurable via the time-range input.\n\n- **Peak users / Peak capacity % / Peak temperature** \u2014 max within the activation window across each metric.\n- **WiFi associations** \u2014 total `count` of `eventType=\"DEVICE_ASSOCIATION\" event=\"ASSOCIATE\"` events.\n- **Spaces \u2014 occupancy surge + Op Florida Ready annotations** \u2014 hourly total occupancy (area chart) with the three exercise dates marked.\n- **Webex \u2014 temperature & humidity during activation** \u2014 avg temp + humidity on the same hourly axis.\n- **Spaces \u2014 WiFi associations by SSID + exercise annotations** \u2014 hourly assoc count stacked by SSID, top 10.\n- **Surge multiplier (single value)** \u2014 `avg(people) during exercise window / avg(people) during prior baseline week`. \u2265 2.0 means the activation roughly doubled the on-site population.\n- **Same metrics, side-by-side** \u2014 bar comparing baseline vs exercise for people / unique users / unique devices.\n\n> **Why some windows are dynamic**: panels that compare \"exercise vs baseline\" use `strptime` hardcoded windows (`2026-04-13` \u2192 `2026-04-16` exercise, `2026-04-06` \u2192 `2026-04-13` baseline) so they remain stable regardless of the dashboard's time-range input. Panels that visualize \"during the activation\" use the dashboard's time-range input so analysts can probe different sub-windows.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 5 \u2014 Visitor Intelligence\n\nSource: `cisco:spaces:firehose eventType=DEVICE_ASSOCIATION` + `DEVICE_PRESENCE`.\n\n- **Unique devices** \u2014 `dc(deviceAssociation.device.macAddress)` over the window.\n- **Repeat visitors %** \u2014 `(devices seen on \u2265 2 distinct days) / total devices * 100`.\n- **Inter-campus travelers** \u2014 devices whose `devicePresence` events include more than one BUILDING. Used as the Sankey input.\n- **Guest vs employee (pie)** \u2014 SSID-based: any SSID matching `(?i)guest` is Guest; everything else is Employee.\n- **Daily visitors with 7-day forecast** \u2014 `predict` on the daily unique-device count; projects 7 days forward.\n- **Guest vs employee by day** \u2014 same SSID classification, daily association counts.\n- **Dwell time distribution** \u2014 per-MAC, per-day association window: `latest(_time) - earliest(_time)`. Bucketed 0-15 m / 15 m-1 h / 1-4 h / 4 h+.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 6 \u2014 Network Impact\n\nPulls in DNAC alongside Spaces so a single timeline shows what the network was doing while people were on it.\n\n- **Network health / Client health (single value, 0-100)** \u2014 DNAC `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` `category=\"All\"` and `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` `clientType=\"ALL\" scoreType=\"ALL\"`, hourly latest, 2-decimal rounded.\n- **Active DNAC issues** \u2014 `dc(IssueID)` from `cisco:dnac:issue`.\n- **Compliance rate** \u2014 `count(eval(ComplianceStatus=\"COMPLIANT\"))/count` of `cisco:dnac:compliance`.\n- **Spaces \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 occupancy + DNAC issues** \u2014 hourly occupancy column chart; high-severity DNAC issues drawn as overlay markers; exercise dates annotated.\n- **DNAC \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 network & client health + DNAC issues** \u2014 both health series + issue overlay on one timeline.\n- **Spaces \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 occupancy vs. client-health scatter** \u2014 one dot per hour. Negative slope = \"more people, worse network.\"\n- **Spaces \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 occupancy + RSSI overlay** \u2014 hourly assoc count (column) + avg `connection.rssi` (line). Does signal degrade with crowd?\n- **Client health by site over time** \u2014 `health.overallScore` per site, per hour.\n- **Spaces \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 occupancy + onboarding-time overlay** \u2014 hourly assoc count + avg onboarding-time.\n- **DNAC issues by severity stacked + occupancy overlay** \u2014 stacked-bar of issue severity (HIGH/MED/LOW) with occupancy line.\n- **AP health distribution (pie)** \u2014 APs grouped by `latest(OverallHealth)`: Excellent (9-10) / Good (7-8) / Fair (5-6) / Poor (0-4).\n- **Client radio band split** \u2014 `connection.band` distribution (2.4 vs 5 GHz).\n- **DNAC issues by site** \u2014 `dc(IssueID)` per `SiteName`.\n- **AP detail table** \u2014 per-AP latest health, CPU %, mem %, issue count, client counts per band, air quality.\n\n---\n\n## Color coding (table cells)\n\nA subset of tables across the dashboard suite uses cell-background tints to highlight what needs attention. Palette is dark-mode-safe (rgba):\n\n- \ud83d\udd34 **Critical** `rgba(214,69,80,0.35)` \u2014 needs attention now (Unreachable, Unmanaged, NON_COMPLIANT, P1, Critical CPU/memory).\n- \ud83d\udfe0 **Warning** `rgba(229,168,35,0.30)` \u2014 watch (Managed With Errors, P2, Warning CPU/memory, At-Risk site).\n- \ud83d\udfe2 **Healthy** `rgba(110,190,74,0.15)` \u2014 subtle green tint (Reachable, Managed, P3/P4, OK).\n\nCurrently colored on **this** dashboard: none \u2014 Spaces tables are mostly numeric ranges. We can add tier coloring to AP detail and Room utilization tables in a follow-up if useful.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\nTo keep page-load performance reasonable, **42 of the 63 panels chain off five base searches** (one `ds.search` per source-type/eventType combination, then `ds.chain`-extended per panel):\n\n- **`ds_base_device_count`** \u2014 `eventType=DEVICE_COUNT inferredLocationTypes=FLOOR` \u2014 13 panels chained.\n- **`ds_base_webex_telemetry`** \u2014 `eventType=WEBEX_TELEMETRY` \u2014 8 panels chained.\n- **`ds_base_device_association`** \u2014 `eventType=DEVICE_ASSOCIATION event=ASSOCIATE` \u2014 7 panels chained.\n- **`ds_base_space_occupancy`** \u2014 `eventType=SPACE_OCCUPANCY` \u2014 7 panels chained.\n- **`ds_base_dnac_issue`** \u2014 `sourcetype=cisco:dnac:issue` \u2014 5 panels chained.\n\nThe remaining 21 panels are inline `ds.search` because they `union`/`appendcols` across multiple sources (e.g., DNAC health + Spaces occupancy on one timeline) and can't share a base.\n\n---\n\n## Known caveats\n\n1. **Field extraction multivalues**: `healthScore` and `scoreValue` from `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` / `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` arrive as multivalue arrays (e.g., `['99','99']`) due to JSON path duplication during indexing. The Network Impact KPIs collapse this with `bin _time | stats latest(field) by _time` rather than `timechart latest(eval(round(...)))` (which silently returns null on multivalues).\n2. **Forecast accuracy**: `predict` panels (capacity 24 h, daily visitors 7 d) need at least ~3 weeks of data for stable projections. With less, the confidence bands will look very wide.\n3. **Op Florida Ready windows are hardcoded** in the activation comparison panels (`2026-04-13` \u2192 `2026-04-16` exercise, baseline = preceding week). Update the `strptime` calls if the exercise dates shift.\n4. **No Meraki, no SD-WAN data in this environment**. Any panel referencing those would be empty by definition; they've been removed across the dashboard suite."
 }
 }
 },
 "dataSources": {
 "ds_act_compare_chart": {
 "name": "Baseline week vs Exercise window - by metric",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" (eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\" OR eventType=\"USER_PRESENCE\" OR eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\")\n| eval phase=case(_time>=strptime(\"2026-04-13 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") AND _time<strptime(\"2026-04-16 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"Exercise (Apr 13-15)\",\n _time>=strptime(\"2026-04-06 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") AND _time<strptime(\"2026-04-13 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"Baseline (week before)\")\n| where isnotnull(phase)\n| eval metric=case(eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\", \"People in buildings (avg/hr)\",\n eventType=\"USER_PRESENCE\", \"Unique users (per event)\",\n eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\", \"Unique devices (per event)\")\n| eval value=case(eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\", 'deviceCounts.associatedCount',\n eventType=\"USER_PRESENCE\", 1,\n eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\", 1)\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats sum(value) as value by phase metric _time\n| stats avg(value) as value by phase metric\n| eval value=round(value, 2)\n| xyseries metric phase value",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "-30d@d",
 "latest": "now"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_act_compare_kpi": {
 "type": "ds.search",
 "name": "Spaces baseline \u00d7 exercise \u2014 surge multiplier",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\"\n| eval people='deviceCounts.associatedCount'\n| where isnotnull(people) AND people>0\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(people) as people by _time\n| eval phase=case(_time>=strptime(\"2026-04-13 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") AND _time<strptime(\"2026-04-16 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"exercise\",\n _time>=strptime(\"2026-04-06 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") AND _time<strptime(\"2026-04-13 00:00:00\",\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"baseline\")\n| where isnotnull(phase)\n| stats avg(people) as avg_people by phase\n| eval avg_people=round(avg_people, 2)\n| xyseries phase phase avg_people\n| eval multiplier=if(isnotnull(baseline) AND baseline>0, round(exercise/baseline, 2), 0)\n| fields multiplier",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_annotation": {
 "name": "2026 key dates annotations",
 "options": {
 "query": "| makeresults count=7\n| streamstats count as id\n| eval _time=case(id=1, strptime(\"2026-04-01 09:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=2, strptime(\"2026-04-10 09:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=3, strptime(\"2026-04-11 09:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=4, strptime(\"2026-04-13 08:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=5, strptime(\"2026-04-14 08:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=6, strptime(\"2026-04-15 08:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n id=7, strptime(\"2026-04-15 18:00:00\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")),\n label=case(id=1, \"Reg / Sponsor deadline\",\n id=2, \"FACHC Refund deadline\",\n id=3, \"Hurricane Prep Workshop\",\n id=4, \"Op Florida Ready - Day 1\",\n id=5, \"Op Florida Ready - Day 2\",\n id=6, \"Op Florida Ready - Day 3\",\n id=7, \"Op Florida Ready - Close\"),\n color=case(id<=3, \"#9E9E9E\",\n id>=4 AND id<=6, \"#D64550\",\n id=7, \"#6EBE4A\")\n| table _time label color",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "01/01/2024:00:00:00",
 "latest": "12/31/2030:23:59:59"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_activation_env": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Webex \u2014 temperature & humidity during activation",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(temp) AND isnotnull(humidity)\n| eval temp_f=round(temp*9/5+32, 2)\n| stats avg(temp_f) as \"Avg Temp \u00b0F\", avg(humidity) as \"Avg Humidity %\", min(temp_f) as \"Min Temp \u00b0F\", max(temp_f) as \"Max Temp \u00b0F\""
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_kpi_capacity": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Peak capacity %",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| stats max(pct) as \"Peak Capacity %\"\n| eval \"Peak Capacity %\"=round('Peak Capacity %', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_kpi_peak": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Peak users",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(users) as peak by _time, floor\n| stats max(peak) as \"Peak Users\""
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_kpi_ssid": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "WiFi associations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_association",
 "query": "| stats count as \"Total Associations\""
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_kpi_temp": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Peak temperature",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(temp)\n| eval temp_f=round(temp*9/5+32, 2)\n| stats avg(temp_f) as \"Avg Temp \u00b0F\"\n| eval \"Avg Temp \u00b0F\"=round('Avg Temp \u00b0F', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_surge": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Spaces \u2014 occupancy surge + Op Florida Ready annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| bin _time span=15m\n| stats max(users) as users by _time, floor, city\n| eventstats avg(users) as baseline_avg, stdev(users) as baseline_std by floor\n| eval surge_threshold=baseline_avg + 2*baseline_std\n| where users > surge_threshold AND users >= 5\n| eval surge_pct=round((users-baseline_avg)/baseline_avg*100, 2)\n| eval _time_str=strftime(_time, \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")\n| table _time_str, city, floor, users, baseline_avg, surge_pct\n| rename _time_str as \"Time\", city as \"City\", floor as \"Floor\", users as \"Users\", baseline_avg as \"Baseline\", surge_pct as \"Surge %\""
 }
 },
 "ds_activation_wifi": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Spaces \u2014 WiFi associations by SSID + exercise annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_association",
 "query": "| timechart useother=t span=1h count as Associations by ssid where max in top10"
 }
 },
 "ds_ap_health_dist": {
 "name": "AP health distribution by tier",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\"\n| stats latest(OverallHealth) as health by DeviceName\n| eval tier=case(health>=9, \"Excellent (9-10)\",\n health>=7, \"Good (7-8)\",\n health>=5, \"Fair (5-6)\",\n health>=1, \"Poor (1-4)\",\n 1=1, \"No Data (0)\")\n| stats count by tier",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_ap_health_table": {
 "name": "AP health detail table",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:devicehealth\" DeviceFamily=\"Unified AP\"\n| stats latest(OverallHealth) as Health,\n latest(CPUUtilization) as \"CPU %\",\n latest(MemoryUtilization) as \"Mem %\",\n latest(IssueCount) as Issues,\n latest(ClientCountGhz24) as \"2.4 GHz Clients\",\n latest(ClientCountGhz50) as \"5 GHz Clients\",\n latest(AirQualityHealthGhz24) as \"Air Quality 2.4\",\n latest(AirQualityHealthGhz50) as \"Air Quality 5\",\n latest(InterferenceHealthGhz24) as \"Interference 2.4\",\n latest(InterferenceHealthGhz50) as \"Interference 5\",\n latest(Site) as Site by DeviceName\n| eval \"Total Clients\"='2.4 GHz Clients'+'5 GHz Clients',\n \"CPU %\"=round('CPU %', 2),\n \"Mem %\"=round('Mem %', 2)\n| sort - \"Total Clients\"\n| rename DeviceName as \"Access Point\"\n| table \"Access Point\", Site, Health, \"CPU %\", \"Mem %\", Issues, \"Total Clients\", \"2.4 GHz Clients\", \"5 GHz Clients\", \"Air Quality 2.4\", \"Air Quality 5\" ",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_band_distribution": {
 "name": "Client band distribution",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\" connectionStatus=\"connected\"\n| eval band='connection.band'\n| where isnotnull(band)\n| stats count by band",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_capacity_gauge_first": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Highest capacity floor (period peak)",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(pct) AND building=\"Tallahassee Headquarters\"\n| stats latest(pct) as \"Capacity %\"\n| eval \"Capacity %\"=round('Capacity %', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_capacity_gauge_second": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Second highest capacity floor (period peak)",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(pct) AND building=\"Tallahassee Operations Center\"\n| stats latest(pct) as \"Capacity %\"\n| eval \"Capacity %\"=round('Capacity %', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_capacity_peak_annotations": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Capacity peak annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(pct) AND pct>=80\n| eval label=\"Capacity \u2265 80% (\".floor.\")\"\n| dedup _time, floor\n| sort - _time\n| head 10\n| table _time label"
 }
 },
 "ds_capacity_predict": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Occupancy forecast (24-hour prediction)",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(users) as users by _time, floor\n| stats sum(users) as users by _time\n| timechart span=1h max(eval(round(users, 2))) as users\n| predict users as predicted future_timespan=24\n| rename \"upper95(prediction(users))\" as upper95,\n \"lower95(prediction(users))\" as lower95\n| eval users=round(users, 2),\n predicted=round(predicted, 2),\n upper95=round(upper95, 2),\n lower95=round(lower95, 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_capacity_trend": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Capacity % by floor over time",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(pct)\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(pct) as pct by _time, floor, building\n| timechart useother=t span=1h max(eval(round(pct, 2))) as \"Capacity %\" by floor where max in top10"
 }
 },
 "ds_client_health_by_site": {
 "name": "Client health score by site over time",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\" connectionStatus=\"connected\"\n| eval site=mvindex(split(siteHierarchy, \"/\"), 3),\n floor=mvindex(split(siteHierarchy, \"/\"), 4),\n health='health.overallScore'\n| where isnotnull(health) AND health>0\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats avg(health) as health by _time, site\n| timechart useother=t span=1h avg(eval(round(health, 2))) as \"Client Health\" by site where max in top10",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_convergence_annotations": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Op Florida Ready exercise annotations (Convergence)",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_dnac_issue",
 "query": "| dedup IssueID\n| eval label=\"DNAC: \".IssueSpecificName.\" - \".SiteName,\n color=\"#D64550\"\n| table _time label color\n| sort - _time\n| head 20"
 }
 },
 "ds_convergence_health": {
 "name": "Convergence health scores",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* (sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\" category=\"All\") OR (sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" clientType=\"ALL\")\n| eval metric=case(sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\", \"network_health\",\n sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\", \"client_health\"),\n value=case(sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\", healthScore,\n sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\", scoreValue)\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats latest(eval(if(metric=\"network_health\", value, null()))) as \"Network Health\",\n latest(eval(if(metric=\"client_health\", value, null()))) as \"Client Health\" by _time\n| eval \"Network Health\"=round('Network Health', 2),\n \"Client Health\"=round('Client Health', 2)",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_convergence_occupancy": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Spaces \u00d7 DNAC \u2014 occupancy + DNAC issues + date annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_device_count",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(users)\n| timechart span=1h max(users) as Occupancy\n| eval Occupancy=round(Occupancy, 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_convergence_timeline": {
 "name": "Convergence Occupancy and Network and Client health",
 "options": {
 "query": "index=* (sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\" category=\"All\") OR (sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\" clientType=\"ALL\") OR (sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\" deviceCounts.location.inferredLocationTypes{}=FLOOR)\n| eval metric_type=case(sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\", \"network_health\",\n sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\", \"client_health\",\n sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\", \"occupancy\"),\n value=case(sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:networkhealth\", healthScore,\n sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:clienthealth\", scoreValue,\n sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\", 'deviceCounts.userCount')\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(eval(if(metric_type=\"occupancy\", value, null()))) as Occupancy,\n latest(eval(if(metric_type=\"network_health\", value, null()))) as \"Network Health\",\n latest(eval(if(metric_type=\"client_health\", value, null()))) as \"Client Health\" by _time\n| eval Occupancy=round(Occupancy, 2),\n \"Network Health\"=round('Network Health', 2),\n \"Client Health\"=round('Client Health', 2)",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_dnac_issue_annotations": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "DNAC high-severity issue annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_dnac_issue",
 "query": "| eval label=IssueSpecificName.\" - \".SiteName\n| dedup IssueID\n| table _time label"
 }
 },
 "ds_dwell_distribution": {
 "name": "Dwell time distribution",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" eventType=\"DEVICE_ASSOCIATION\"\n| eval mac='deviceAssociation.device.macAddress',\n event='deviceAssociation.event'\n| sort mac, _time\n| streamstats current=f last(event) as prev_event, last(_time) as prev_time by mac\n| where event=\"DISASSOCIATE\" AND prev_event=\"ASSOCIATE\"\n| eval dwell_min=round((_time-prev_time)/60, 2)\n| eval bucket=case(dwell_min<30, \"< 30 min\",\n dwell_min<60, \"30-60 min\",\n dwell_min<120, \"1-2 hrs\",\n dwell_min<240, \"2-4 hrs\",\n dwell_min<480, \"4-8 hrs\",\n 1=1, \"8+ hrs\")\n| stats count by bucket\n| rename bucket as \"Dwell Time\" ",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_env_annotation": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Op Florida Ready exercise annotations (Environmental)",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(temp) AND isnotnull(humidity)\n| eval temp_f=round(temp*9/5+32, 2)\n| where temp_f >= 78 OR humidity >= 65\n| eval label=case(temp_f>=78, \"Heat \".round(temp_f, 0).\"\u00b0F\", humidity>=65, \"Humidity \".round(humidity, 0).\"%\")\n| dedup _time, label\n| sort - _time\n| head 10\n| table _time label"
 }
 },
 "ds_env_kpi_humidity": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Avg humidity",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(humidity)\n| timechart span=1h avg(humidity) as \"Humidity %\"\n| eval \"Humidity %\"=round('Humidity %', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_env_kpi_temp": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Avg temperature",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(temp)\n| eval temp_f=round(temp*9/5+32, 2)\n| timechart span=1h avg(temp_f) as \"Temp \u00b0F\"\n| eval \"Temp \u00b0F\"=round('Temp \u00b0F', 2)"
 }
 },
 "ds_env_occupancy_overlay": {
 "name": "Occupancy vs temperature overlay",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" (eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\" OR eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\")\n| eval users=if(eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\", 'deviceCounts.userCount', null()),\n temp=if(eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\", 'webexTelemetryUpdate.telemetries{}.ambientTemp', null())\n| where isnotnull(users) OR isnotnull(temp)\n| eval temp_f=if(isnotnull(temp), round(temp*9/5+32, 2), null())\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(users) as Users, avg(temp_f) as temp_avg by _time\n| eval Users=round(Users, 2),\n \"Temperature (F)\"=round(temp_avg, 2)\n| fields _time Users \"Temperature (F)\" ",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_env_scatter": {
 "name": "Temperature vs users scatter",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" (eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\" OR eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\")\n| eval users=if(eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\", 'deviceCounts.userCount', null()),\n temp=if(eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\", 'webexTelemetryUpdate.telemetries{}.ambientTemp', null())\n| where isnotnull(users) OR isnotnull(temp)\n| eval temp_f=if(isnotnull(temp), round(temp*9/5+32, 2), null())\n| bin _time span=1h\n| stats max(users) as users, avg(temp_f) as temp_f by _time\n| where isnotnull(users) AND isnotnull(temp_f)\n| eval users=round(users, 2), temp_f=round(temp_f, 2)\n| table users temp_f",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_env_summary": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Current sensor readings",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(temp) AND isnotnull(humidity)\n| eval temp_f=round(temp*9/5+32, 2)\n| stats avg(temp_f) as avg_temp, avg(humidity) as avg_humidity, count\n| eval comfort=case(avg_temp>=68 AND avg_temp<=76 AND avg_humidity>=30 AND avg_humidity<=60, \"\u2713 Optimal\",\n avg_temp>76 OR avg_humidity>60, \"\u26a0 Warm/Humid\",\n 1=1, \"\u2717 Cool/Dry\")\n| eval avg_temp=round(avg_temp, 1), avg_humidity=round(avg_humidity, 1)\n| table comfort, avg_temp, avg_humidity, count\n| rename comfort as \"Comfort\", avg_temp as \"Avg Temp \u00b0F\", avg_humidity as \"Avg Humidity %\", count as \"Readings\""
 }
 },
 "ds_humidity_trend": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "Webex sensors \u2014 humidity by floor + exercise annotations",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_webex_telemetry",
 "query": "| where isnotnull(humidity) AND isnotnull(device)\n| timechart span=1h avg(humidity) as \"Humidity %\" by device limit=10"
 }
 },
 "ds_inter_campus": {
 "name": "KPI Inter-campus travelers",
 "options": {
 "query": "`index_spaces` sourcetype=\"cisco:spaces:firehose\" eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\"\n| eval mac='devicePresence.macAddress'\n| eval bldg_self=if(mvfind('devicePresence.location.inferredLocationTypes{}', \"BUILDING\")>=0, 'devicePresence.location.name', null())\n| eval bldg_parent=if(mvfind('devicePresence.location.parent.inferredLocationTypes{}', \"BUILDING\")>=0, 'devicePresence.location.parent.name', null())\n| eval bldg_grand=if(mvfind('devicePresence.location.parent.parent.inferredLocationTypes{}', \"BUILDING\")>=0, 'devicePresence.location.parent.parent.name', null())\n| eval building=coalesce(bldg_self, bldg_parent, bldg_grand)\n| where isnotnull(mac) AND mac!=\"\" AND isnotnull(building) AND building!=\"\"\n| stats dc(building) as buildings by mac\n| where buildings>1\n| stats count as \"Inter-Campus Travelers\" ",
 "queryParameters": {
 "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
 "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
 }
 },
 "type": "ds.search"
 },
 "ds_issues_by_site": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "DNAC \u2014 issues by site",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_dnac_issue",
 "query": "| dedup IssueID\n| stats count as Issues by SiteName\n| sort - Issues\n| rename SiteName as Site"
 }
 },
 "ds_issues_timeline": {
 "type": "ds.chain",
 "name": "DNAC issues by severity timeline",
 "options": {
 "extend": "ds_base_dnac_issue",
